  "Number": 12,
  "Question": "The ratio of the number of games won to the number of games lost (no ties) by the Middle School Middies is \\(\\frac{11}{4}.\\) To the nearest whole percent, what percent of its games did the team lose?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(24\\%\\)",
    "B": "\\(27\\%\\)",
    "C": "\\(36\\%\\)",
    "D": "\\(45\\%\\)",
    "E": "\\(73\\%\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "The ratio gives \\(11\\) parts wins for every \\(4\\) parts losses. Since there are no ties, all games together make \\(11+4=15\\) equal ratio parts, of which \\(4\\) are losses.\n\nThus the percentage of games lost is\n\\[\n\\frac4{15}\\cdot100\\%=26.666\\ldots\\%.\n\\]\nRounding to the nearest whole percent gives \\(27\\%\\), choice \\(\\text{B}\\).",
